{"kind":"report","text":"Read MemexRL including training, rewards and modified ALFWorld evaluation, and checked TTRL and Reflexion primary abstracts. Proposed an ordinary room facilitator agent that maintains concise evidence-linked context, predicts near-term problems, proposes bounded steering, and assesses subsequent outcomes. Distinguished inference-time memory and instruction updates from model-weight RL. Proposed evaluating summaries through decisions they support, preserving pre-outcome predictions, testing frozen historical contexts without future leakage, and measuring live benefit and human overhead. Paper evidence supports memory management, not causal improvement of multi-party rooms. No new protocol vocabulary or source changes."}